---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Contact — A3S Labs" description="Start a conversation with A3S Labs about product engineering, applied AI, infrastructure, education technology or experimental systems." canonicalPath="/contact">
  <section class="contact-hero section-pad">
    <div class="shell contact-hero-grid">
      <div class="contact-hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span>CONTACT</span><span>A3S / 05</span></p>
        <h1>Bring the problem, not a buzzword list.</h1>
        <p>A useful conversation starts with the system you need to build, fix, understand or validate. A3S Labs is most relevant where software has a real data path, operational constraint or technical unknown behind the interface.</p>
      </div>

      <aside class="contact-route-card" aria-label="Public contact routes">
        <div class="contact-route-head"><span>PUBLIC ROUTES</span><span>02 CHANNELS</span></div>
        <div class="contact-route-list">
          <a href="https://github.com/simlexx-k" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
            <span>01</span><span><b>GitHub</b><small>Repositories, issues and technical work</small></span><span>↗</span>
          </a>
          <a href="https://x.com/simlexx0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
            <span>02</span><span><b>X / @simlexx0</b><small>Public conversation and direct outreach</small></span><span>↗</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-pad section-rule">
    <div class="shell">
      <header class="section-heading split-heading">
        <div><p class="section-kicker">Good fit</p><h2>Work where the engineering matters.</h2></div>
        <p>The portfolio is deliberately broad, but the common thread is end-to-end system ownership: inputs, models, APIs, runtime, deployment and the user-facing surface.</p>
      </header>

      <div class="contact-fit-grid">
        <article><span>01</span><h3>Product engineering</h3><p>Web/mobile systems, APIs, data models, background workflows and production delivery where the whole path needs to work together.</p></article>
        <article><span>02</span><h3>Applied AI + data</h3><p>Extraction, classification, forecasting, computer vision and decision-support systems tied to measurable signals and explicit uncertainty.</p></article>
        <article><span>03</span><h3>Infrastructure + operations</h3><p>Docker/VPS systems, observability, secure service boundaries, deployment recovery and operator-facing tooling.</p></article>
        <article><span>04</span><h3>Research prototypes</h3><p>Technical experiments that need a route from data and evaluation into a reproducible API, interface or operational proof.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-pad detail-band">
    <div class="shell narrative-grid">
      <div><p class="section-kicker">Before reaching out</p><h2>Useful context gets to the hard part faster.</h2></div>
      <div class="narrative-copy">
        <p>Include the problem, who uses the system, the data or external services involved, the current technical state, the most important constraint and what a successful outcome would look like.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="/products">Review products <span>↗</span></a>
          <a class="button button-quiet" href="/engineering">Engineering approach</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-pad section-rule">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="contact-note">No simulated contact form, fictional office details or response-time promise is published here. The public routes above are the channels currently tied to the actual work.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
